Package: open-vm-tools-wayland
Architecture: amd64
Provides: open-vm-tools
Conflicts: open-vm-tools
Replaces: open-vm-tools
Depends:
 coreutils,
 iproute2,
 pciutils,
 procps,
 sed,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Open Virtual Machine Tools for VMware guests, with native Wayland support
 open-vm-tools supplies the guest-side drivers and agents that let a VMware
 guest report its status to the host, synchronise its clock, resize its
 display, and share the clipboard and dragged files with the host.
 .
 This build is the upstream 13.1.0 release plus the Wayland work: clipboard
 and drag-and-drop over the Wayland data-control protocols, and pointer
 integration through the XDG RemoteDesktop portal and libei. The X11 paths are
 unchanged and are still used in an X11 session.
 .
 It installs the same binaries and plugins as the distribution package, so it
 replaces it rather than living beside it.

Package: open-vm-tools-wayland-desktop
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 open-vm-tools-wayland (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Provides: open-vm-tools-desktop
Conflicts: open-vm-tools-desktop
Replaces: open-vm-tools-desktop
Description: Desktop integration plugins for open-vm-tools-wayland
 The per-user plugins that run inside the desktop session: clipboard and
 drag-and-drop, automatic display resizing, and the VMware tools autostart
 entry. Install this on a guest with a graphical session.
